      "repair": "Either add the second message to the seed (with a real MCP-deployment-status question authored by an existing user, consistent with existing timestamps/IDs) so the referent set genuinely contains two matches, or abandon the 'multiple' resolution_mode and keep this as a single-referent case matching slack_66's actual data."
    },
    {
      "kind": "validity",
      "location": "assignment.resolution_mode vs actual seed content",
      "problem": "resolution_mode is 'multiple' and route/referent_entity are set up for a plural reply target, but the only real, currently-seeded matching message is the single 1700173200.000456. The multiplicity is manufactured purely by inventing an unseeded row rather than by discovering true plurality in existing data.",
      "repair": "Ground the plural referent in the real seed by adding a bona fide second MCP-deployment question consistent with domain constraints, or change resolution_mode/task back to single to match the true data."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The design plan hinges on a second target message (1700200000.000457) that is not present in the base_seed messages array supplied with the case, while the assignment explicitly states base_seed is 'unchanged.' This means the compiled task's core referent set cannot be satisfied by the actual seed data — the solver would only ever find one genuine MCP-deployment question in #general, not the required two. This is a fabricated-data defect, not a stylistic concern, and invalidates the plurality this mutation is built around. The negative roles (engineering rewrite, DM, growth CDN question, general watch-party/captcha messages) are otherwise well-chosen and topically distinct, but they cannot compensate for the missing/fabricated positive referent that the obligation depends on."
